\ Two modules export `probe`, and both bodies are directly reachable and
\ compilable. Module A's `a-probe` calls A's `probe`; the entry file imports B's.
\ Each module's word gets its own compiled function, so A's call site reaches A's
\ body rather than whichever `probe` won the bare name at discovery.

use { a-probe: } "fixtures/aot_module_word_identity_a.1z" ;
use { probe: } "fixtures/aot_module_word_identity_b.1z" ;

a-probe print-line
probe print-line
